SUBTRACTIVE QUALIFICATION

D2_SUBTRACTIVE_SLOW,
D3_SUBTRACTIVE_SLOW,
D2_SUBTRACTIVE_MEDIUM,
or D3_SUBTRACTIVE_MEDIUM
is A40-PRESSURE-QUALIFIED iff all are true:

1. overall oscillation <= 5%;

2. biased-periodic oscillation <= 10%;

3. breaks at least 50%
   of paired OPP_SLOW biased-periodic oscillators;

4. biased-periodic oscillation
   is less than paired MARGIN_SLOW;

5. balanced false-majority <= 10%;

6. balanced false-majority
   is less than paired ZERO_CROSS_SLOW;

7. reversal acquisition >= 80%;

8. median old-majority loss <= 4 epochs;

9. aggregate service >= 90%
   of paired OPP_SLOW;

10. false C dominance
    does not exceed paired OPP_SLOW;

11. false S dominance
    does not exceed paired OPP_SLOW;

12. recruitment remains nondegenerate;

13. all integrity probes pass.

A40_INFORMATION_GAIN

TRUE iff at least one SUBTRACTIVE arm:

reduces biased-periodic oscillation
versus paired MARGIN_SLOW;

breaks at least 25%
of paired OPP_SLOW biased-periodic oscillators;

has balanced false-majority
below paired ZERO_CROSS_SLOW;

retains reversal acquisition >= 80%;

retains >= 90% paired OPP_SLOW service;

and exhibits either:

positive pre-pulse-M / defection-latency correlation;

or

greater epoch-2 core persistence
in the high-M quartile
than the low-M quartile.

MECHANISM ATTRIBUTION

If SUBTRACTIVE succeeds
where MARGIN fails
without ZERO_CROSS stickiness:

support credit is useful,
but it must act directly on opposing pressure
rather than only enlarge K.

If SUBTRACTIVE behaves like MARGIN:

direct credit spending is still too permissive,
and the missing mechanism is not
a simple pressure transform.

If SUBTRACTIVE behaves like ZERO_CROSS_SLOW:

the subtraction creates an effective hard gate
and is too restrictive.

If MEDIUM succeeds but SLOW is sticky:

the pressure transform is useful
but slow temporal memory remains excessive.

If both SUBTRACTIVE arms fail
despite clear local erosion ordering:

the remaining population oscillator
is not solvable by committed-state
pressure shaping alone.

